[
  {
    "id": "LINUX-101",
    "level": 1,
    "title": "Exploration et Arborescence Système",
    "topic": "Navigation & Fichiers de Base",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "points": 2.0,
    "description": "### Exploration du Répertoire Courant\n\nAffichez le chemin absolu du répertoire dans lequel vous vous trouvez avec `pwd`, puis listez l'ensemble des fichiers y compris les fichiers cachés avec `ls -la`.\n\n#### Objectif\n- Exécuter `pwd`\n- Exécuter `ls -la`",
    "starter_cmd": "# Tapez vos commandes de navigation\n",
    "solution": "pwd && ls -la",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          ".bashrc": { "type": "file", "content": "# bashrc config\n" },
          ".profile": { "type": "file", "content": "export PATH\n" },
          "documents": { "type": "dir", "files": {} },
          "notes.txt": { "type": "file", "content": "Bienvenue sur Linux\n" }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Affichage chemin absolu",
        "cmd": "pwd",
        "expected_stdout": "/home/student",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "/home/student"
      },
      {
        "name": "Affichage fichiers cachés",
        "cmd": "ls -la",
        "expected_stdout": ".bashrc",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": ".bashrc"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification enchaînement pwd et ls",
        "cmd": "pwd && ls -a",
        "expected_stdout": "/home/student",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "/home/student"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification présence notes.txt",
        "cmd": "ls -l notes.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "notes.txt",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "notes.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Navigation relative documents",
        "cmd": "cd documents && pwd",
        "expected_stdout": "/home/student/documents",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "/home/student/documents"
      },
      {
        "name": "Navigation répertoire parent",
        "cmd": "cd .. && pwd",
        "expected_stdout": "/home",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "/home"
      },
      {
        "name": "Filtrage fichier note",
        "cmd": "ls -la | grep notes.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "notes.txt",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "notes.txt"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Utilisez la commande 'pwd' pour afficher le répertoire courant.",
      "L'option '-la' de 'ls' combine l'affichage long et les fichiers masqués."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-102",
    "level": 1,
    "title": "Création d'une Structure de Projet",
    "topic": "Navigation & Fichiers de Base",
    "difficulty": "easy",
    "points": 2.0,
    "description": "### Création d'Arborescence\n\nCréez les répertoires `project/src` et `project/docs` à l'aide de `mkdir -p`, puis initialisez les fichiers vides `project/src/main.sh` et `project/README.md` avec `touch`.\n\n#### Objectif\n- `mkdir -p project/src project/docs`\n- `touch project/src/main.sh project/README.md`",
    "starter_cmd": "# Créez l'arborescence et les fichiers requis\n",
    "solution": "mkdir -p project/src project/docs && touch project/src/main.sh project/README.md",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {}
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification répertoire project/src",
        "cmd": "test -d project/src && echo 'SRC_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "SRC_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "project/src"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification fichier README.md",
        "cmd": "test -f project/README.md && echo 'README_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "README_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "project/README.md"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification répertoire docs",
        "cmd": "test -d project/docs && echo 'DOCS_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "DOCS_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "project/docs"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification script main.sh",
        "cmd": "test -f project/src/main.sh && echo 'MAIN_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "MAIN_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "project/src/main.sh"
      },
      {
        "name": "Listing récursif du projet",
        "cmd": "ls -R project",
        "expected_stdout": "main.sh",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "main.sh"
      },
      {
        "name": "Test intégrité README",
        "cmd": "ls project | grep README.md",
        "expected_stdout": "README.md",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "README.md"
      },
      {
        "name": "Test présence sous-dossiers",
        "cmd": "ls project | grep src",
        "expected_stdout": "src",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "src"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "L'option '-p' de 'mkdir' crée les répertoires parents manquants si nécessaire.",
      "La commande 'touch fichier' permet de créer un fichier vide sans ouvrir d'éditeur."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-103",
    "level": 1,
    "title": "Copie, Renommage et Suppression",
    "topic": "Navigation & Fichiers de Base",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "points": 3.0,
    "description": "### Manipulation de Fichiers\n\n1. Copiez l'ensemble du dossier `reports` vers `reports_backup` avec `cp -r`.\n2. Déplacez/renommez `draft.txt` vers `archive/old_draft.txt` avec `mv`.\n3. Supprimez le fichier temporaire `temp.log` avec `rm`.",
    "starter_cmd": "# Commandes cp, mv et rm\n",
    "solution": "cp -r reports reports_backup && mv draft.txt archive/old_draft.txt && rm temp.log",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "reports": {
            "type": "dir",
            "files": {
              "q1.txt": { "type": "file", "content": "Q1 Report\n" }
            }
          },
          "archive": { "type": "dir", "files": {} },
          "draft.txt": { "type": "file", "content": "Brouillon initial\n" },
          "temp.log": { "type": "file", "content": "Trace temporaire à détruire\n" }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification dossier reports_backup",
        "cmd": "test -d reports_backup && echo 'BACKUP_DIR_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "BACKUP_DIR_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "reports_backup"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification suppression temp.log",
        "cmd": "test ! -f temp.log && echo 'TEMP_REMOVED'",
        "expected_stdout": "TEMP_REMOVED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_not_exists",
        "expected": "temp.log"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Contenu du backup copié",
        "cmd": "test -f reports_backup/q1.txt && echo 'REPORT_COPIED'",
        "expected_stdout": "REPORT_COPIED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "reports_backup/q1.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification déplacement archive/old_draft.txt",
        "cmd": "test -f archive/old_draft.txt && echo 'DRAFT_ARCHIVED'",
        "expected_stdout": "DRAFT_ARCHIVED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "archive/old_draft.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification absence de draft.txt d'origine",
        "cmd": "test ! -f draft.txt && echo 'ORIGIN_MOVED'",
        "expected_stdout": "ORIGIN_MOVED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_not_exists",
        "expected": "draft.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Contenu intègre dans old_draft",
        "cmd": "cat archive/old_draft.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "Brouillon initial",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_contains",
        "expected": "Brouillon initial"
      },
      {
        "name": "Préservation du dossier reports source",
        "cmd": "test -f reports/q1.txt && echo 'SRC_INTACT'",
        "expected_stdout": "SRC_INTACT",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "reports/q1.txt"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Pour copier un répertoire récursivement, utilisez 'cp -r'.",
      "La commande 'mv source destination' déplace et renomme simultanément."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-201",
    "level": 2,
    "title": "Sécurisation des Permissions d'Exécution",
    "topic": "Permissions & Sécurité",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "points": 3.0,
    "description": "### Sécurisation POSIX\n\n1. Attribuez les permissions `755` (`rwxr-xr-x`) au script `deploy.sh`.\n2. Restreignez le fichier sensible `secrets.env` avec les permissions `600` (`rw-------`).",
    "starter_cmd": "# Modifiez les permissions des fichiers\n",
    "solution": "chmod 755 deploy.sh && chmod 600 secrets.env",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "deploy.sh": { "type": "file", "content": "#!/bin/bash\necho 'Deploying...'\n", "mode": "644" },
          "secrets.env": { "type": "file", "content": "DB_PASSWORD=secret_super_token\n", "mode": "644" }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Permissions deploy.sh",
        "cmd": "test -x deploy.sh && echo 'EXEC_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "EXEC_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "permission",
        "expected": "755"
      },
      {
        "name": "Droits secrets.env",
        "cmd": "ls -l secrets.env",
        "expected_stdout": "secrets.env",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "permission",
        "expected": "600"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification statut binaire deploy.sh",
        "cmd": "stat -c %a deploy.sh 2>/dev/null || ls -l deploy.sh | grep -E 'rwxr-xr-x|755'",
        "expected_stdout": "deploy.sh",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "deploy.sh"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification restriction secrets.env",
        "cmd": "stat -c %a secrets.env 2>/dev/null || ls -l secrets.env | grep -E 'rw-------|600'",
        "expected_stdout": "secrets.env",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "secrets.env"
      },
      {
        "name": "Exécution deploy.sh",
        "cmd": "./deploy.sh",
        "expected_stdout": "Deploying...",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "Deploying..."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lecture secrets.env propriétaire",
        "cmd": "cat secrets.env",
        "expected_stdout": "DB_PASSWORD",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_contains",
        "expected": "DB_PASSWORD"
      },
      {
        "name": "Listing permissions combinées",
        "cmd": "ls -l deploy.sh secrets.env",
        "expected_stdout": "deploy.sh",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "deploy.sh"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "En notation octale : 7 (rwx), 5 (r-x), 0 (---).",
      "'chmod 755 script' donne lecture/exécution à tous et écriture au seul propriétaire."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-202",
    "level": 2,
    "title": "Filtrage et Recherche avec Grep et Find",
    "topic": "Filtrage Textuel",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "points": 3.0,
    "description": "### Recherche & Filtrage de Contenu\n\n1. Filtrez les erreurs 'CRITICAL' dans `service.log` et affichez les lignes correspondantes avec leur numéro de ligne via `grep -n`.\n2. Trouvez tous les fichiers `.log` dans `/var/log` avec la commande `find`.",
    "starter_cmd": "# Utilisez grep et find\n",
    "solution": "grep -n 'CRITICAL' service.log && find /var/log -name '*.log'",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "service.log": {
            "type": "file",
            "content": "INFO: Booting\nCRITICAL: Memory leak detected at 0x4f\nINFO: Running\nCRITICAL: Process crashed\nDEBUG: End\n"
          }
        }
      },
      "/var/log": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "syslog.log": { "type": "file", "content": "syslog ok\n" },
          "auth.log": { "type": "file", "content": "auth ok\n" }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Extraction lignes CRITICAL",
        "cmd": "grep -n 'CRITICAL' service.log",
        "expected_stdout": "CRITICAL: Memory leak",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "CRITICAL: Memory leak"
      },
      {
        "name": "Numéro de ligne grep",
        "cmd": "grep -n 'CRITICAL' service.log",
        "expected_stdout": "2:",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "2:"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Seconde erreur CRITICAL",
        "cmd": "grep -n 'CRITICAL' service.log",
        "expected_stdout": "4:",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "4:"
      },
      {
        "name": "Comptage des occurrences CRITICAL",
        "cmd": "grep -c 'CRITICAL' service.log",
        "expected_stdout": "2",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "2"
      },
      {
        "name": "Recherche find des fichiers .log",
        "cmd": "find /var/log -name '*.log'",
        "expected_stdout": "syslog.log",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "syslog.log"
      },
      {
        "name": "Recherche find auth.log",
        "cmd": "find /var/log -name '*.log'",
        "expected_stdout": "auth.log",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "auth.log"
      },
      {
        "name": "Inversion grep non critique",
        "cmd": "grep -v 'CRITICAL' service.log",
        "expected_stdout": "INFO: Booting",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "INFO: Booting"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "L'option '-n' de 'grep' préfixe chaque ligne trouvée par son numéro de ligne.",
      "La commande 'find /chemin -name '*.ext'' recherche les fichiers selon leur motif de nom."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-301",
    "level": 3,
    "title": "Pipeline d'Analyse de Logs et Redirection",
    "topic": "Pipes & Redirections",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "points": 4.0,
    "description": "### Tubes et Redirections de Flux\n\nAnalysez le fichier d'accès HTTP `access.log` : extrayez toutes les requêtes ayant le code `404`, comptez le nombre de lignes via `wc -l`, et enregistrez ce total dans `404_count.txt` à l'aide d'une redirection `>`.",
    "starter_cmd": "# Combinez grep, wc -l et la redirection >\n",
    "solution": "grep ' 404 ' access.log | wc -l > 404_count.txt",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "access.log": {
            "type": "file",
            "content": "127.0.0.1 - - [20/Oct/2026] \"GET /index.html\" 200 452\n10.0.0.2 - - [20/Oct/2026] \"GET /missing.png\" 404 120\n10.0.0.3 - - [20/Oct/2026] \"POST /login\" 200 500\n10.0.0.4 - - [20/Oct/2026] \"GET /unknown.php\" 404 120\n10.0.0.5 - - [20/Oct/2026] \"GET /admin/broken\" 404 120\n"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Création du fichier 404_count.txt",
        "cmd": "test -f 404_count.txt && echo 'FILE_CREATED'",
        "expected_stdout": "FILE_CREATED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "404_count.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Contenu du compteur",
        "cmd": "cat 404_count.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "3",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_contains",
        "expected": "3"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Vérification valeur exacte",
        "cmd": "tr -d ' ' < 404_count.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "3",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "3"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification lignes 404 originales",
        "cmd": "grep ' 404 ' access.log",
        "expected_stdout": "missing.png",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "missing.png"
      },
      {
        "name": "Vérification exclusion 200",
        "cmd": "grep -v ' 404 ' access.log",
        "expected_stdout": "index.html",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "index.html"
      },
      {
        "name": "Test non vide du fichier résultat",
        "cmd": "test -s 404_count.txt && echo 'NON_EMPTY'",
        "expected_stdout": "NON_EMPTY",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "NON_EMPTY"
      },
      {
        "name": "Pipeline complet sans redirection",
        "cmd": "grep ' 404 ' access.log | wc -l",
        "expected_stdout": "3",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "3"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "Le symbole '|' (pipe) connecte la sortie standard d'une commande à l'entrée standard de la suivante.",
      "La redirection '>' écrit le flux dans le fichier cible en écrasant son contenu préalable."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-302",
    "level": 3,
    "title": "Chaînage Conditionnel et Enchaînements",
    "topic": "Scripts Bash",
    "difficulty": "hard",
    "points": 4.0,
    "description": "### Enchaînements Logiques (&&, ||)\n\nVérifiez si le fichier `config.json` existe avec `test -f config.json` :\n- Si oui : écrivez 'CONFIG_OK' dans `status.txt` via `&&`.\n- Si non : créez `config.json` avec `{}` et enregistrez 'CONFIG_CREATED' dans `status.txt` via `||`.",
    "starter_cmd": "# Utilisez test -f, && et ||\n",
    "solution": "test -f config.json && echo 'CONFIG_OK' > status.txt || (echo '{}' > config.json && echo 'CONFIG_CREATED' > status.txt)",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/home/student": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {}
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Création du fichier status.txt",
        "cmd": "test -f status.txt && echo 'STATUS_EXISTS'",
        "expected_stdout": "STATUS_EXISTS",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "status.txt"
      },
      {
        "name": "Message de création",
        "cmd": "cat status.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "CONFIG_CREATED",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_contains",
        "expected": "CONFIG_CREATED"
      }
    ],
    "hidden_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Présence de config.json généré",
        "cmd": "test -f config.json && echo 'CONF_FILE_OK'",
        "expected_stdout": "CONF_FILE_OK",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_exists",
        "expected": "config.json"
      },
      {
        "name": "Contenu de config.json",
        "cmd": "cat config.json",
        "expected_stdout": "{}",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "file_contains",
        "expected": "{}"
      },
      {
        "name": "Test d'idempotence après création",
        "cmd": "test -f config.json && echo 'EXISTS'",
        "expected_stdout": "EXISTS",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "EXISTS"
      },
      {
        "name": "Code de retour de test",
        "cmd": "test -f status.txt; echo $?",
        "expected_stdout": "0",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "0"
      },
      {
        "name": "Taille de status.txt",
        "cmd": "wc -l < status.txt",
        "expected_stdout": "1",
        "expected_exit_code": 0,
        "assertion_type": "stdout",
        "expected": "1"
      }
    ],
    "hints": [
      "'cmd1 && cmd2' n'exécute cmd2 que si cmd1 réussit (code retour 0).",
      "'cmd1 || cmd2' exécute cmd2 si cmd1 échoue (code retour différent de 0)."
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "LINUX-401",
    "level": 4,
    "title": "Gestion des Processus et Signaux Système",
    "topic": "Processus & Signaux",
    "difficulty": "very_hard",
    "points": 5.0,
    "description": "### Signaux et Processus\n\nUn processus consommateur anormal nommé `miner_daemon` tourne sur le PID `4096`. Identifiez-le avec `ps`, envoyez-lui un signal d'arrêt forcé `SIGKILL` avec `kill -9 4096`, puis vérifiez avec `ps` qu'il n'apparaît plus.",
    "starter_cmd": "# Inspectez les processus et terminez le PID ciblé\n",
    "solution": "ps aux | grep miner_daemon && kill -9 4096",
    "initial_fs": {
      "/proc": {
        "type": "dir",
        "files": {
          "processes.json": {
            "type": "file",
            "content": "[{\"pid\": 1, \"cmd\": \"systemd\"}, {\"pid\": 4096, \"cmd\": \"miner_daemon\"}, {\"pid\": 5001, \"cmd\": \"bash\"}]"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "public_tests": [
      {
        "name": "Détection du processus rogue",
